# Reviewed, dated exceptions for the M7 Trivy blocking-policy pass
# (TTLI_Code_report.md M7; docs/STATUS.md §10 has the original clamav-
# debian review this pass builds on). Every entry below was individually
# checked against real `trivy image --format json` output on 2026-08-28,
# after fixing everything this repo actually controls (see the fix:
# report M7 commits immediately before this file was added -- an
# openssl point-release bump in apps/api/Dockerfile, stripping the
# unused bundled npm CLI from apps/web's runtime stage, and bumping
# mailpit six tag-versions to current). What's left is either an
# upstream package Debian/Alpine hasn't patched yet, or a binary
# embedded in a third-party image this repo only pulls and doesn't
# build. `exp:2026-11-26` (90 days out): once an entry expires, Trivy
# stops honouring it and the CVE goes back to failing the build --
# forces a real re-check instead of a permanent exception. Regenerate
# with the same JSON-diffing approach documented in the M7 commits
# rather than re-typing this by hand.

